      "committer": {
        "name": "dylanoliverdo-coder",
        "email": "265406556+dylanoliverdo-coder@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T13:38:28Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): the field simulator cuts a move past the per-move ceiling in pieces, so Stock cuts what the column engine cuts\n\nNo caller segmented a chord whose swept window passes MAX_CELLS_PER_MOVE,\nso through Stock the field engine refused ordinary moves: a 12.7 mm\nendmill's 300 mm pass, a 127 mm tool's 6 mm plunge, an undercut disc's\n6 mm plunge. SdfField::subtract_batch_fitted cuts such a chord or arc\npiece as the fewest equal pieces that each pass the ceiling (doubling,\nthen bisection; it refuses when pieces of one cell still pass it). The\nfield arms of Stock (simulate_field_with, simulate_undercut, the lathe\nand display arms) cut through it; subtract_batch keeps the refusal as\nthe bound of one update. The #4079 pin moves to subtract_batch directly.\n\nFixes #4179\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
