      "committer": {
        "name": "dylanoliverdo-coder",
        "email": "265406556+dylanoliverdo-coder@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-27T01:45:52Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): the single-move Stock arms cut in pieces too; an unsplittable sweep refuses by name (#4179 review)\n\nPre-review of #4267:\n\n- `Stock::subtract_flat` and `Stock::cut_chord` still called the\n  refusing `SdfField::subtract` on the field arm. Both now cut through\n  `subtract_batch_fitted`, so all six field arms of `Stock` split a\n  move past the ceiling. Pin: `the_single_move_stock_arms_cut_the_long_chord`.\n- `fit` gave no pieces, and so cut nothing, for a sweep that is neither\n  a chord nor an arc piece. It now refuses by name. No caller builds\n  such a sweep today.\n- `a_wide_tools_long_chord_still_refuses_and_its_segments_cut` ran past\n  60 s in debug (three mesh-built fields, two cuts). It now builds the\n  block with `SdfField::from_box` and cuts the chord once.\n- Wording: travel \"exceeds\" the ceiling and the pieces \"fall under\" it,\n  one word for each meaning. The decision file follows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
